    "text": "Traditional theories of autobiography, such as Philippe Lejeune's autobiographical pact, focus on the relationship between author, narrator, and protagonist within a retrospective written account of personal experience.",
    "topic": "autobiographical theory"
  },
  {
    "text": "The study examines how selfhood may be constructed beyond written individual life narratives by analyzing oral autobiographical voice in the folktales of Kweku Ananse and Kweku Tsin.",
    "topic": "oral autobiography"
  },
  {
    "text": "Anansesɛm, a component of Akan oral tradition, involves the character Kweku Ananse engaging in autobiographical storytelling.",
    "topic": "Akan oral tradition"
  },
  {
    "text": "The Autobiographical Voice of Kweku Ananse explores self-representation, storytelling, and narrative authority within Akan oral tradition.",
    "topic": "self-representation"
  },
  {
    "text": "The study of the Autobiographical Voice of Kweku Ananse focuses on memory and self-representation in storytelling.",
    "topic": "memory"
  }
